# generated: font subsets copied out of @fontsource-variable/inter
web/public/fonts/

# generated: plain-JS copy of lib/ui/core/format/, compiled by
# tsconfig.parity.json so the codepoint parity check can run on a Node that
# vitest refuses to install on. Build output, never committed.
web/dist-parity/

# A Claude session working directory that keeps appearing at the repository
# root (.claude/ settings + a scheduled-tasks lock + .seed-shots/). FW32
# deleted it once under R264 and it came back. Ignored rather than removed:
# it is not this repository's, and R334 forbids deleting what a session did
# not create.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH (FW-FOLLOWUP). Unanchored, this pattern
# matches a directory of that name at ANY depth - and git's ignore matching is
# case-INSENSITIVE here (core.ignorecase=true on Windows), so it was silently
# ignoring every Kotlin source directory under
# android/*/src/*/kotlin/ch/monreleve/. Already-tracked files were unaffected,
# because .gitignore does not apply to tracked paths; only NEW ones vanished,
# which is the worst version of this bug - nothing fails, the file is simply
# not in the commit. Found when this task's CodeCopyTest.kt would not stage.
# The comment above says "at the repository root", so the anchor is what was
# meant all along.
/MonReleve/

# R349: the per-worktree session lock. Operational state, never repository
# content - it was committed once by a `git add -A` run from web/, which
# stages the whole repository and not the current directory.
.session-lock.json

# R1038: a worktree's keep marker. web/scripts/wt-cleanup.mjs reads
# C:/wt/<task>/.wt-keep as "merged, but its evidence is still needed" and
# prints its content as the reason. Ignored so a kept worktree stays clean;
# the script also exempts it in worktrees checked out before this line.
# Anchored at the root, where the script reads it (FW-FOLLOWUP's lesson).
/.wt-keep

# KMP-2: the on-device walkthrough screenshots, and Kotlin's build cache.
#
# Every device task writes its PNGs to android/.<task>-shots/ - the helper
# android/scripts/uidrive.mjs puts them there. Seventeen such directories had
# accumulated untracked, so every `git status` in this repository opened with a
# screen of them and a real untracked file had to be spotted among the noise.
# That is how FW-VERIFY came to delete an operator file it had misread as its
# own: a status listing nobody can read is a status nobody checks.
#
# ANCHORED AND SUFFIX-MATCHED (FW-FOLLOWUP's lesson, one pattern over): the
# leading slash keeps this at android/ rather than any depth, and `-shots`
# cannot collide with a source directory the way an unanchored `MonReleve/`
# did. The screenshots are evidence FOR A REPORT, not repository content: they
# are read while the task runs and quoted in the report afterwards.
/android/.*-shots/

# Kotlin 2.x's incremental build cache. Build output, never committed.
/android/.kotlin/

# IOS-2b: a device session's evidence folder at the repository root (/.<task>-evidence/).
# It holds the local dev server's log, which carries sign-in links and codes (R574), so
# it is ignored by rule rather than kept out by staging-by-name alone. Anchored at the
# root and suffix-matched, the /android/.*-shots/ shape one directory up.
/.*-evidence/
